  "summary": {},
  "notes": [
    "ROW ALIGNMENT VERIFIED: the page-1 scan is rotated, so the General Fund, SEF and Total figures appear to sit about one row below their labels (most visibly in the expenditure block). Each block has exactly as many figures as labels, the last figure sits in the last grid row, and every row checks out (e.g. Education GF 7,186,764.96 + SEF 1,311,561.90 = Total 8,498,326.86; the six expenditure items sum to the printed 405,075,275.25; RPT GF 106,455,037.54 + SEF 92,362,854.81 = 198,817,892.35). Values are therefore assigned to the row of the label they belong to, not shifted.",
    "Printed NET INCREASE/(DECREASE) IN FUNDS (GF) is 406,833,320.38, but Net Operating Income (GF) 788,765,323.45 minus Total Non-Operating Expenditures 115,064.07 is 788,650,259.38. The difference, 381,816,939.00, equals the Internal Revenue Allotment for the quarter, so the form appears to have left the IRA out of this line; FUND/CASH AVAILABLE and FUND/CASH BALANCE, END (GF and Total) carry the lower figure forward. Transcribed as printed.",
    "Printed NET OPERATING INCOME (LOSS) Total 497,999,677.36 does not equal GF + SEF (788,765,323.45 + 91,051,292.91 = 879,816,616.36); it equals GF net operating income less the IRA (406,948,384.45) + SEF. Transcribed as printed.",
    "Printed FUND/CASH BALANCE, END (GF) 2,611,921,805.29 is 0.34 more than the arithmetic of the printed column (2,611,921,804.95); Prior Year Payables target 366,792,931.84 vs Total 366,792,932.18 also differ by 0.34. Transcribed as printed.",
    "Blank cells (SEF items, target column for expenditures, all non-income receipt rows) are null; printed \"-\" is 0. Labels are kept as printed, including typos. The NTA line is printed as \"Internal Revenue Allotment\".",
    "This quarter has no GF/SEF reconciliation table and no Total Assets line."
  ],
